---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import LegalShell from '../components/legal/LegalShell.astro';
import { legalPage } from '../data/legal';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';

const page = legalPage(
  'privacy-policy',
  '/privacy-policy/',
  'Privacy Policy | Tip Top Hybrid',
  'What Tip Top Hybrid collects through this website, our estimate forms and phone calls, how we use it, and the choices California residents have.',
);
---

<BaseLayout page={page}>
  <LegalShell title="Privacy Policy" updated="November 15, 2026">
    <p>
      <strong>Tip Top Hybrid</strong> (“we”, “us”, “our”) runs <strong>www.tiptophybrid.com</strong> and
      the hybrid repair shop at {SITE.street}, Upland, CA 91786. This policy explains what we collect
      through the website, our estimate and contact forms, and calls or texts to the shop, and the
      choices you have. It does not cover other companies’ websites.
    </p>

    <h2>1. What we collect</h2>
    <p><strong>What you give us.</strong> When you submit a form, call, text or email us, we collect:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Your name, email address and phone number;</li>
      <li>Your vehicle’s year, make and model, and the symptoms or service you describe;</li>
      <li>Anything else you choose to write in the message field or tell us.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      <strong>Collected automatically.</strong> Our hosting, analytics and advertising tools record
      your IP address, approximate location, device and browser type, referring page, the pages you
      view, and how you interact with them (clicks, scrolling, form starts).
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Calls.</strong> Calls to the numbers on this site may be routed through a call-tracking
      service that logs which page or ad produced the call, plus the date, time and duration. We do
      not record call audio unless we tell you at the start of the call.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not ask for payment card details, government ID numbers or health information through
      this site, and you should not send them through a form.
    </p>

    <h2>2. How we use it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Reply to your request, prepare an estimate and schedule service;</li>
      <li>Contact you by phone, text or email about your enquiry and your vehicle;</li>
      <li>Keep records of the estimates, repairs and warranties we provide;</li>
      <li>Measure how the site and our advertising perform so we can improve them;</li>
      <li>Protect against spam, fraud and misuse of the site; and</li>
      <li>Meet our legal, tax and record-keeping obligations.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Cookies, analytics and advertising</h2>
    <p>
      We use <strong>Google Tag Manager</strong> to load the tools below. These tools use cookies,
      pixels and device identifiers to collect the information described in section 1:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Google Analytics 4</strong> — measures traffic and how visitors use the site
        (aggregated reporting).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Google Ads</strong> — measures which ads and clicks lead to enquiries, and may show
        our ads to people who have visited the site (remarketing). Under California law, remarketing
        can count as “sharing” personal information for cross-context behavioural advertising.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Microsoft Clarity</strong> — records session replays, heatmaps and click analytics so
        we can see where visitors get stuck. Clarity captures clicks, scrolling and page interactions.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Google call tracking</strong> — lets us see which page or ad a call came from, which
        may involve showing a different tracking number while you browse.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Google Maps</strong> — the map embedded on our pages is served by Google, which may
        set its own cookies when the map loads.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>You can limit this:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Block or delete cookies in your browser settings.</li>
      <li>
        Turn off personalised Google ads at
        <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Google Ads Settings</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        Install the
        <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Google Analytics opt-out add-on</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        Use the industry opt-outs at
        <a href="https://optout.networkadvertising.org" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">NAI</a> or
        <a href="https://optout.aboutads.info" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">DAA</a>.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Blocking cookies does not stop you from using the site or requesting an estimate.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Who we share it with</h2>
    <p>We do not sell your personal information, and we do not share it with third parties for their own marketing.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Service providers</strong> that run the site and its tools: our hosting and content
        delivery provider, our form-handling provider, Google (analytics, ads, call tracking, maps),
        and Microsoft (Clarity). They may only use the data to provide those services to us.
      </li>
      <li><strong>Our staff and technicians</strong>, to answer your enquiry and work on your vehicle.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Legal or safety disclosures</strong> where required by law, court order, or to protect
        our rights, property or someone’s safety.
      </li>
      <li><strong>A buyer or successor</strong> if the business is sold, merged or transferred.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>5. Calls and texts</h2>
    <p>
      By giving us your phone number, you agree that we may call, text or email you about your
      enquiry. Message and data rates may apply. Reply <strong>STOP</strong> to stop texts or
      <strong>HELP</strong> for help, or tell us on the call that you would prefer another contact
      method. Consent to calls or texts is not a condition of getting an estimate or service. We do
      not add your number to a marketing text list without your consent.
    </p>

    <h2>6. How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>
      We keep enquiry and repair records for as long as needed for the purposes above — including
      warranty, accounting and legal requirements — and then delete or anonymise them.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Security</h2>
    <p>
      We use reasonable administrative and technical safeguards to protect the information we hold.
      No method of transmission over the internet or electronic storage is completely secure, so we
      cannot guarantee absolute security.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Your California privacy rights</h2>
    <p>
      If you live in California, the California Consumer Privacy Act (as amended by the CPRA) gives
      you the right to:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Know what personal information we have collected, used and disclosed about you;</li>
      <li>Request a copy of it;</li>
      <li>Ask us to delete or correct it;</li>
      <li>
        Opt out of the “sale” or “sharing” of personal information — we do not sell personal
        information; advertising cookies used for remarketing may count as “sharing”, and you can opt
        out using the links in section 3 or by contacting us;
      </li>
      <li>Limit our use of sensitive personal information — we do not collect sensitive personal information through this site; and</li>
      <li>Not be treated differently for exercising these rights.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      To make a request, call <strong>{SITE.phone}</strong> or email
      <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> with “Privacy request” in the subject line. We
      may ask for information to verify your identity first. An authorised agent can make a request
      for you with your written permission. We aim to respond within 45 days.
    </p>
    <p>
      California’s “Shine the Light” law also lets California residents ask whether we have disclosed
      personal information to third parties for their direct marketing — we do not do this.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Children</h2>
    <p>
      The site is intended for adults. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children
      under 13. If you think a child has sent us information, contact us and we will delete it.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Other websites</h2>
    <p>
      The site links to third-party sites such as Google Maps and social media. Their privacy
      practices are governed by their own policies.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy from time to time. The date at the top shows when it last changed, and
      the version posted here applies from that date.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Contact us</h2>
    <p>
      Tip Top Hybrid<br />
      {SITE.street}, Upland, CA 91786<br />
      Phone: <strong>{SITE.phone}</strong><br />
      Email: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>
    </p>
  </LegalShell>
</BaseLayout>
